1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,950
Lesson 29: resize and recentre

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:15,164
YA-NEC course, lesson 29: Resize and recentre, new in 1.5.3. First, Segments per lambda for MMANA files: 160.

3
00:00:15,214 --> 00:00:48,852
Examples: the I4GBZ 11-element Yagi for 144 MHz, an MMANA file.

4
00:00:48,902 --> 00:01:11,742
In MMANA it gives 51.4 + j4.5 ohm at 144.300 MHz. In NEC-2, 5 m over average ground: 7.3 - j14.1 ohm, SWR 7.4. A very narrow-band antenna: the length offset between MININEC and NEC-2, about 0.4 %, is enough to move it.

5
00:01:11,792 --> 00:01:20,159
Variables and optimization, Resize and recentre.

6
00:01:20,209 --> 00:01:34,132
Two modes. Recentre: find where the antenna works best now and move it to the target frequency. Resize: from one frequency to another, for example a 144 MHz design moved to 50 MHz.

7
00:01:34,182 --> 00:01:42,855
Diameters: scaled, equal, or commercial sizes, with solid rods from 3 to 6 mm and rods or tubes from 8 to 40 mm.

8
00:01:42,905 --> 00:01:49,322
And the check box: zero the reactance, X = 0, with the driven element length only.

9
00:01:49,372 --> 00:01:54,481
Recentre at 144.3 MHz with equal diameters: Search.

10
00:01:54,531 --> 00:02:08,687
The SWR minimum is now at 143.766 MHz: factor 0.9963, every element shortened by 3-4 mm; the driven element trimmed by 3.1 mm.

11
00:02:08,737 --> 00:02:30,945
Result at 144.3 MHz: before 7.3 - j14.1 ohm, SWR 7.44; after 53.5 - j0.0 ohm, SWR 1.07, 21.69 dBi, F/B 13.1 dB. The reactance is zero, the R stays the antenna's own.

12
00:02:30,995 --> 00:02:40,384
Commercial sizes, and Search again.

13
00:02:40,434 --> 00:02:57,318
Nothing changes here: 6 and 12 mm are already commercial sizes. With an odd diameter each element takes the nearest enabled size and the length is corrected for the same reactance, with Schelkunoff's line model, like the Leeson correction.

14
00:02:57,368 --> 00:03:03,318
So far the open model has not changed: see first, decide later.

15
00:03:03,368 --> 00:03:23,069
Apply and recalculate.

16
00:03:23,119 --> 00:03:34,344
The recentred model opens and is calculated: the antenna now works at 144.3 MHz in NEC-2 too. The file on disk does not change: save it with Save as.

17
00:03:34,394 --> 00:03:41,267
The other mode: resize, from one frequency to another.

18
00:03:41,317 --> 00:03:53,401
It scales around the lowest point, so the height above ground stays; L and C loads are not scaled. Geometry, Scale remains the generic tool with a hand-written factor.

19
00:03:53,451 --> 00:04:02,502
Resize and recentre: an MMANA model or a design moved to the right frequency in one click, with real diameters. 73 de IC8TEM
